  "verifiedSupportingConclusion": {
    "status": "RESERVED_UNREACHABLE",
    "summary": "authority-utils.js's annotateAuthorityCandidates() does assign a genuine authorityRole:'SUPPORTING' value to non-governing candidates when at least one GOVERNING peer exists, and pipeline.js calls it (line ~3376) on ctx.rerankedChunks. However, this per-candidate role is not confirmed to survive, unambiguously and consistently, through every finalSourceCards assignment branch to the API surface trust-contract.js consumes (displayedSourceCount/sourceCards), and wiring it in would require a new, non-trivial aggregation rule (e.g. 'SUPPORTING only if every displayed card is non-governing') that is a distinct design decision beyond this conflict-focused correction's scope. Per this task's explicit instruction not to expand the patch beyond the conflict correction and not to manufacture a classification from weak/indirect evidence, VERIFIED_SUPPORTING remains reserved but unreachable. This is the most concrete lead for a future, separately-scoped task."
